            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for chalk, then the Kannada for a ruler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹೆದರು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೆದರು — hedaru — \"to be afraid; to fear\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮಗು ಕತ್ತಲೆಗೆ ಹೆದರುತ್ತದೆ. magu kattalege hedaruttade. The child is afraid of the dark."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಹೆದರಿದೆ, hedaride."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What you fear takes -ಗೆ: ಕತ್ತಲೆಗೆ ಹೆದರು (hedaru), to be afraid of the dark. The noun for the feeling is ಭಯ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೆದರು (hedaru) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4401 lists Kannada bedaṟu and hedaṟu, \"to be alarmed, to take fright\", with a noun meaning \"fright\" beside them. The b- and h- forms are two shapes of one old verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
