          "title": "You'll want to know: ನಾಚು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾಚು — nācu — \"to feel shy; to be bashful\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹೊಸ ಅತಿಥಿಯನ್ನು ನೋಡಿ ಹುಡುಗಿ ನಾಚಿದಳು. hosa atithiyannu nōḍi huḍugi nācidaḷu. Seeing the new guest, the girl felt shy."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ನಾಚಿದೆ, nācide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun beside it is ನಾಚಿಕೆ, shyness: the verb is the feeling happening, the noun is the feeling itself."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾಚು (nācu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 3639 gives Kannada nāṇcu, nāñcu and nācu, \"to become abashed\", beside a noun for bashfulness and modesty."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
