        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಆತಂಕ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆತಂಕ — ātaṅka — \"anxiety; dread\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪರೀಕ್ಷೆಗೆ ಮೊದಲು ನನಗೆ ಆತಂಕ ಆಯಿತು. parīkṣege modalu nanage ātaṅka āyitu. Before the exam I felt anxious."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feeling takes the dative of the person: ನನಗೆ ಆತಂಕ (ātaṅka) ಆಯಿತು, I grew anxious."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಆತಂಕ (ātaṅka) is borrowed from Sanskrit ātaṅka, which Monier-Williams gives first as a sickness of the body and then as affliction of mind, disquiet and fear (Monier-Williams). Kannada keeps the second sense: the dread before something happens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
